27:20.120 --> 27:23.940
against, we were taunted that more electronic vehicles were coming, and then we were also

27:24.440 --> 27:27.780
blamed that our delegate's speech had taken

27:28.280 --> 27:31.980
up someone else's precious time. I will now segue to that right turn

27:32.060 --> 27:36.460
ban and why it is erroneous in nature

27:36.960 --> 27:41.560
and ill-conceived. As the region of Waterloo policies are

27:42.060 --> 27:45.600
causing the harm to pedestrians.

27:45.760 --> 27:49.400
Shoehorning roundabouts into four-lane all directional artery roads, as was done at

27:49.900 --> 27:53.599
Ottawa Westmount, is dangerous loss of pedestrian

27:54.099 --> 27:57.560
safety convention. I wish everybody safety, but that

27:58.060 --> 28:02.320
intersection will now be the added statistics of region of Waterloo

28:02.720 --> 28:06.080
putting people in harm's way.

28:06.500 --> 28:10.140
Roundabouts work well in rural

28:10.640 --> 28:14.340
crossroads and solve vehicle collisions. In dense urban

28:14.980 --> 28:18.860
use, they put pedestrians in peril. A visually impaired

28:19.360 --> 28:22.940
person is allowed to ride the Grand River Transit system,

28:23.440 --> 28:27.100
no charge, but must now attempt to cross a roundabout with

28:27.600 --> 28:31.420
removed crossing signals. School children and shoppers and people who live near

28:31.920 --> 28:35.500
that intersection will now be unsure of their travels. Planning that puts

28:36.000 --> 28:39.100
people first has been hijacked by removing

28:39.600 --> 28:43.740
safety signals, then claiming the removal is ideal and sustainable.

28:44.240 --> 28:48.300
People do not have to sustain this thinking and these

28:48.800 --> 28:52.900
actions on our personal safety. Our rights

28:53.400 --> 28:56.380
to movement are innate under law. My application of those principles traces all the way

28:56.880 --> 29:00.540
back to the Magna

29:01.040 --> 29:04.820
Carta. Region of Waterloo has changed the nature of drivers. Drivers now race into

29:05.120 --> 29:08.510
roundabouts, only looking left and only looking right when

29:09.010 --> 29:12.550
it can be too late for a pedestrian who's crossing.

29:12.950 --> 29:16.870
This has set to the need for band-aid

29:17.370 --> 29:21.590
reactions and of course the deflected blame that right turns are considered the

29:22.070 --> 29:25.590
culprit to people's crosswalk safety. I know region of Waterloo

29:26.090 --> 29:30.190
has some big files and issues on their hands, water, snow clearing, transit revenue declines

29:30.690 --> 29:34.220
and a freeze on development. Transportation is important. And intertwines through all of

29:34.720 --> 29:38.020
those issues. The fact remains, pedestrians walk out of their house,

29:38.260 --> 29:41.740
they step onto transit, they walk into schools or businesses,

29:42.240 --> 29:46.180
or any brick and mortar location. Pedestrians are not going away, they are

29:46.680 --> 29:50.220
intrinsic to everything. This is precisely why our sidewalks and trails

29:50.720 --> 29:54.660
must be protected from the proliferation of electric vehicles, placing rental scooters on sidewalks

29:54.740 --> 29:58.540
at transit

29:59.040 --> 30:02.120
intersections, is irresponsible and contrary to bylaw.

30:02.200 --> 30:06.120
It sends signals to private scooter owners that sidewalks

30:06.280 --> 30:10.360
are their domain. In October, while driving

30:10.860 --> 30:14.400
on Union Street at Belmont, a rented scooter and an e-motorcycle came

30:14.900 --> 30:18.720
directly into the road from the trail. They did

30:19.220 --> 30:22.040
not stop to press the flashing light for me to stop for pedestrians. They just

30:22.540 --> 30:26.200
came onto the road. Luckily, no collision, nor damage

30:26.700 --> 30:30.470
to my vehicle, nor attempt to try to blame me

30:30.970 --> 30:34.910
through a dysfunctional bylaw and road safety system. These vehicles

30:35.410 --> 30:39.150
should not be on the trail. They should

30:39.650 --> 30:43.430
be on the road following the Highway Traffic Act.

30:43.930 --> 30:47.710
This is an issue of massive

30:48.210 --> 30:51.830
legal implication. Reports and news stories that these e-scooter rentals contribute to the local economy

30:52.330 --> 30:54.150
is pure propaganda. Working in merchant credit card processing and gift cards and loyalty programs

30:54.650 --> 30:58.580
for 26 years, I know merchant marketing and

30:59.080 --> 31:02.620
engagement for retailers, and I know that e-scooters

31:03.260 --> 31:05.380
do nothing for businesses in uptown. The e-scooters are used in parallel to transit service,

31:05.880 --> 31:16.860
so the loss of transit rider revenue is the economic reality. The e-scooter operator

31:17.980 --> 31:18.527
contract is void if passengers or bags of groceries or baskets are affixed onto a

31:19.027 --> 31:20.300
scooter. The e-scooters are used to go out to bars.

31:22.710 --> 31:24.550
Arnold, you have about 30 seconds.

31:25.350 --> 31:29.270
We hear the carnage nine floors up on King

31:29.770 --> 31:33.350
Street, uptown. We hear it all.

31:33.850 --> 31:37.710
We see all the scooters, sometimes laying in the road

31:38.210 --> 31:41.190
or near the train tracks. There is no economic spin-off, only a degraded community.

31:41.690 --> 31:45.230
We demand an immediate revamp of trail and sidewalk bylaws. We demand the

31:45.730 --> 31:49.470
removal of these e-scooters laying across our sidewalks. We demand an immediate pivot

31:49.970 --> 31:53.780
towards a pedestrian right-of-way bylaw system that protects and enhances people's right

31:54.280 --> 31:58.540
to and use of our walkways. We demand that these motorized vehicles be used under

31:59.040 --> 32:02.900
license and liability insurance required or they are relegated to private property

32:03.400 --> 32:07.060
use only. Thank you. Thank you. Hanging on there, Arnold, Chair Redmond,

