01:20:26.880 --> 01:20:30.790
out there and we're excited to work with partners

01:20:31.290 --> 01:20:35.190
to look at different funding mechanisms to do just

01:20:35.690 --> 01:20:40.030
that. So I'd say, yeah, focusing on EV charging will be a big

01:20:40.530 --> 01:20:44.350
push and then looking for financing mechanisms. Sorry. And then just my

01:20:44.850 --> 01:20:48.190
comment toward 8.2.2 for the benefit of my council

01:20:48.690 --> 01:20:52.510
colleagues is just that I think this is really important to support for the benefit

01:20:53.010 --> 01:20:56.240
of seven generations beyond all of us. And I,

01:20:56.740 --> 01:21:00.120
even if you don't think of it that way, just the financial benefit of a

01:21:00.620 --> 01:21:04.120
15% retrofit versus a 1% addition to a new build

01:21:04.620 --> 01:21:07.880
is good finance. So thank you for

01:21:08.380 --> 01:21:12.200
sharing that in the

01:21:12.700 --> 01:21:16.440
report today. Councillor Wolfe, you're up. Through you, Madam Chair, again, thank you

01:21:16.940 --> 01:21:20.960
for your reports. Just curious, where does the region generate most

01:21:21.460 --> 01:21:25.510
of its carbon? Through our buildings or through our transportation? Through the chair

01:21:26.010 --> 01:21:29.630
and thank you for that question.

01:21:30.130 --> 01:21:34.750
Currently our largest source of corporate emissions is related

01:21:35.250 --> 01:21:39.070
to transit, so GRT. Now we tend to sort of bracket GRT though

01:21:39.790 --> 01:21:43.390
because yes they are high in

01:21:43.890 --> 01:21:47.510
terms of corporate emissions but they are driving down community emissions in a positive way.

01:21:48.010 --> 01:21:52.040
So we always have to we have to be careful when

01:21:52.540 --> 01:21:56.480
we put that forward. Next to transit then comes buildings. That is our

01:21:56.980 --> 01:22:00.760
second highest source of emissions. Okay. And in the Zero

01:22:00.920 --> 01:22:04.580
Carbon Building Design Award, I know

01:22:05.080 --> 01:22:08.320
in Cambridge we always were gold leads.

01:22:08.820 --> 01:22:11.720
How would it compare to, let's say, a platinum leads?

01:22:12.220 --> 01:22:15.110
Or do they measure different things? Yes,

01:22:15.610 --> 01:22:20.110
through the chair. Thank you for that question. Yes, they are slightly

