01:34:47.200 --> 01:34:50.800
The guiding principles we'll promote as we

01:34:51.040 --> 01:34:54.280
renew and updates the regional forest management plan are illustrated in simple form here to

01:34:54.780 --> 01:34:57.706
protect, enhance, restore, expand and connect. Informed by these principles, we will be drafting the

01:34:58.206 --> 01:35:00.360
new 10-year regional forest management plan that will address the emerging priorities shown here on

01:35:00.860 --> 01:35:04.070
the right side of your screen. The plan will

01:35:04.570 --> 01:35:08.230
place a focus on integrating a regional forest

01:35:08.730 --> 01:35:11.670
as critical infrastructure assets in the corporate asset management plan.

01:35:12.170 --> 01:35:15.790
We will identify opportunities to build resilience to a changing climate.

01:35:16.290 --> 01:35:19.510
In order to ensure we can respond to the growing pressures these forests are facing,

01:35:20.010 --> 01:35:23.390
we are developing a program growth model to forecast

01:35:23.890 --> 01:35:27.110
changing conditions and identify necessary investments needed to meet targeted levels of

01:35:27.610 --> 01:35:30.980
