02:16:46.380 --> 02:16:49.660
And we're moving on to other business. Councillor Funic.

02:16:50.140 --> 02:16:53.580
Thank you, Chair James. This other business

02:16:53.740 --> 02:16:57.700
is with respect to Mobility Plus seat belts or lap

02:16:58.200 --> 02:17:02.880
belts policy. In recent weeks, I received communication

02:17:03.380 --> 02:17:07.000
from two separate mobility plus passengers who,

02:17:07.080 --> 02:17:11.560
to my knowledge, didn't know each other and were very distressed

02:17:11.720 --> 02:17:16.560
when they were waiting and ready for their ride. And they were told

02:17:17.060 --> 02:17:20.360
by the driver that they were unable to board because they didn't

02:17:20.860 --> 02:17:24.760
have seat belts on their wheelchair. This was particularly

02:17:24.840 --> 02:17:28.110
distressing as it occurred without warning for them,

02:17:28.190 --> 02:17:31.550
these passengers had been riding for weeks

02:17:31.790 --> 02:17:33.550
and months respectively.

02:17:34.830 --> 02:17:38.270
And so I found it particularly surprising

02:17:38.590 --> 02:17:42.590
because I know from experience that all mobility plus buses

02:17:42.749 --> 02:17:46.590
are equipped with lap belts and shoulder

02:17:47.090 --> 02:17:50.990
straps. And I was told that it was

02:17:51.490 --> 02:17:55.609
communicated to these customers that they are to procure

02:17:55.849 --> 02:17:59.849
their own lap belts. And I think that is particularly

02:17:59.929 --> 02:18:03.489
problematic for safety concerns, as we

02:18:03.989 --> 02:18:07.929
don't have a way to monitor quality in that sense.

02:18:08.329 --> 02:18:11.449
Also, we heard from Dr.

02:18:11.849 --> 02:18:15.529
Mathers this morning that in many contexts,

02:18:16.249 --> 02:18:19.920
a seat belt is seen as

02:18:20.420 --> 02:18:24.580
a restraint which is not allowed in various

02:18:24.820 --> 02:18:28.580
institutions. So I just want to make sure that

02:18:29.080 --> 02:18:32.820
our safety policies are aligned

02:18:32.980 --> 02:18:36.780
across the region and that the passengers who

02:18:37.280 --> 02:18:40.980
are customers who rely on them are fully aware

02:18:41.480 --> 02:18:44.780
of them. Commissioners, can you Speak to this,

02:18:45.020 --> 02:18:48.300
please. Yes, through you, Chair. Councillor Hunick,

02:18:48.800 --> 02:18:51.060
thank you for this and all the questions that you bring forward. And I will

02:18:51.560 --> 02:18:53.620
tell you, I'm going to be very measured in my response. This is not my

02:18:54.120 --> 02:18:56.780
lived experience and I have a bit of learning to do. So, I'm going to

02:18:57.280 --> 02:18:59.900
first read you the line, the GRT policy line,

02:19:01.100 --> 02:19:04.500
and then I'll offer some thoughts. So, the line reads as follows,

02:19:05.000 --> 02:19:08.580
for the safety of all mobility plus customers traveling with mobility devices, it is essential

02:19:09.080 --> 02:19:12.390
that all devices be kept in good working condition. This includes having

02:19:12.890 --> 02:19:16.870
functional brakes, lap belts, motors and secure structure for proper securement.

02:19:17.370 --> 02:19:21.190
If a mobility aid is unsafe or not mechanically functional, access to book rides

02:19:21.690 --> 02:19:24.230
may be suspended until the issue is resolved. So having said that,

02:19:25.270 --> 02:19:28.310
I will offer today to go away and review and report back.

02:19:29.590 --> 02:19:32.390
I will do that on a timeline of a month of your choosing, but I

02:19:32.890 --> 02:19:35.960
will tell you if we identify a challenge or a policy change that's needed,

02:19:36.460 --> 02:19:38.760
I'll just notify by email and we'll make that change. So we won't wait around

02:19:39.260 --> 02:19:42.280
for a report back, but I do want the opportunity to take it away and

02:19:42.780 --> 02:19:45.280
have a look with my team. Thank you. For the customers that are affected,

02:19:45.440 --> 02:19:49.760
they're waiting with bated breath to

02:19:50.260 --> 02:19:53.840
be reinstated for services. Is it possible for you

02:19:54.340 --> 02:19:58.320
or a member of your team to follow up with them and do

02:19:58.820 --> 02:20:02.060
some public relations, etc., etc.? Yes,

02:20:02.560 --> 02:20:06.820
through your chair, Councillor Hunicke, earlier today, Councillor Wolf referred to transit as a lifeline

02:20:07.320 --> 02:20:10.660
and so I will take that responsibility seriously and we'll follow up with the two

02:20:11.160 --> 02:20:15.060
customers you've identified and anybody else that's been impacted. Thank you. Thank you. Sorry,

02:20:15.560 --> 02:20:17.659
when will the report come back? Sorry, the end.

02:20:19.980 --> 02:20:23.420
Through your chair, why don't we say two months? So we are sitting

02:20:23.920 --> 02:20:26.780
here in March, I will say May, but again, I plan to resolve this a

02:20:27.280 --> 02:20:29.000
lot sooner. Faster than that. Thank you. Thank you.

